OPPORTUNITY COST
"Opportunity Cost is the cost of next best alternative foregone".
For example, suppose you are working in a bank at the salary of
40,000 per month. Further suppose, you receive two more job
offers:
To work as an executive at 30,000 per month; or
• To become a journalist at 35,000 per month.
In the given case, the opportunity cost of working in the bank is
the cost of next best alternative foregone, i.e. 35,000. The
amount of other goods and services, that must be sacrificed to
obtain more of any one good, is called the opportunity cost of
that good
